   "html": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Human Scale in Window Views</title>\n<script type=\"application/json\" id=\"sp-scheme\">\n{\n \"format\": \"sp-scheme-package\",\n \"spScheme\": \"2.0\",\n \"survey\": {\n  \"title\": \"Human Scale in Window Views\",\n  \"description\": \"Faithful replication with the original photographs: two window views of residential neighbourhoods in Ljubljana, Slovenia (N1 Litostrojski bloki, building distance 31.8 m, mostly vertical greenery of tall trees; N2 Štepanjsko naselje, 117.6 m, a large lawn with trees), each photographed from where a resident looks out of the window at the opposite façade. Participants read the paper's definition of human scale (quoted from Ewing and Clemente) and, for each view, choose from the paper's seven indicators: area connectivity, readability and completeness of the ambience, clarity and expressiveness of building design, complementarity of buildings, urban furniture and other areas, presence of greenery, transparency of tree canopies, perception of artistic composition principles. As in the paper's two survey approaches, each participant is randomly given either single choice (one indicator per view, SA1) or multiple choice (any number, SA2). Field of study is asked at the end. Rebuilt from Fikfak, Zbašnik Senegačnik & Drobne (2024), Human-Scale Greenery in the Window View, Urban Science 8(4): 257, with the photographs cropped from its Figure 3 and the definition, indicators and procedure from its Section 2.3 (CC BY 4.0). It is the human-scale part of the same student survey whose imageability part is the template 2022-fikfak-imageability. Image ids: N1, N2; group records SA1 or SA2; answers are in humanscale_single (SA1) or humanscale_multi (SA2), keyed by view. Analysis as in the paper: share of responses for each indicator per view and survey approach, ranks of the indicators, a homogeneity test of the rank differences between the two approaches and the correlation of ranks; the paper (88 architecture and urbanism students) found presence of greenery among the most chosen indicators for both views under both approaches (the most chosen under multiple choice), with readability and completeness of the ambience chosen most often for N2 under single choice. Differences from the original study: (1) the paper's first six questions on the need for a window and the importance of a good view are not included because their wording is not printed; (2) the paper gave the two approaches to two separate student groups (architecture students in a Moodle classroom, urbanism students on 1KA, both online in May 2022); here the approach is randomly assigned and anyone can take part; (3) the question wording, the instruction text and the view order (N1 then N2) are ours; (4) the field-of-study question is ours; (5) the photographs are the figure copies (about 780 px wide).\",\n  \"locale\": \"en\",\n  \"mediaFolders\": [\n   \"views\"\n  ],\n  \"pages\": [\n   {\n    \"name\": \"start\",\n    \"elements\": [\n     {\n      \"type\": \"consent\",\n      \"name\": \"consent\",\n      \"title\": \"I agree to take part. Participation is voluntary and my answers are recorded anonymously for research.\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"labelTrue\": \"I agree\",\n      \"labelFalse\": \"I do not agree\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"type\": \"radiogroup\",\n      \"name\": \"group\",\n      \"title\": \"Survey approach (set by the page)\",\n      \"isRequired\": false,\n      \"visible\": false,\n      \"choices\": [\n       {\n        \"value\": \"SA1\",\n        \"text\": \"single choice\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"SA2\",\n        \"text\": \"multiple choice\"\n       }\n      ]\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"views\",\n    \"elements\": [\n     {\n      \"type\": \"radiogroup\",\n      \"name\": \"humanscale_single\",\n      \"title\": \"Which element gives this window view its human scale?\",\n      \"isRequired\": false,\n      \"choices\": [\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I1\",\n        \"text\": \"Area connectivity\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I2\",\n        \"text\": \"Readability and completeness of the ambience\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I3\",\n        \"text\": \"Clarity and expressiveness of building design\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I4\",\n        \"text\": \"Complementarity of buildings, urban furniture, and other areas\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I5\",\n        \"text\": \"Presence of greenery\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I6\",\n        \"text\": \"Transparency of tree canopies\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I7\",\n        \"text\": \"Perception of artistic composition principles\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"SA1 group: one indicator per view. Keyed by view (N1, N2).\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"type\": \"checkbox\",\n      \"name\": \"humanscale_multi\",\n      \"title\": \"Which elements give this window view its human scale? Choose all that apply.\",\n      \"isRequired\": false,\n      \"choices\": [\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I1\",\n        \"text\": \"Area connectivity\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I2\",\n        \"text\": \"Readability and completeness of the ambience\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I3\",\n        \"text\": \"Clarity and expressiveness of building design\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I4\",\n        \"text\": \"Complementarity of buildings, urban furniture, and other areas\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I5\",\n        \"text\": \"Presence of greenery\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I6\",\n        \"text\": \"Transparency of tree canopies\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I7\",\n        \"text\": \"Perception of artistic composition principles\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"SA2 group: any number of indicators per view. Keyed by view (N1, N2).\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"about\",\n    \"elements\": [\n     {\n      \"type\": \"radiogroup\",\n      \"name\": \"field\",\n      \"title\": \"What is your background?\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"choices\": [\n       {\n        \"value\": \"architecture\",\n        \"text\": \"Architecture (student or professional)\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"urbanism\",\n        \"text\": \"Urbanism / urban planning (student or professional)\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"other_design\",\n        \"text\": \"Another design or environment field\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"other\",\n        \"text\": \"Other\"\n       }\n      ]\n     }\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n }\n}\n</script>\n<script type=\"application/json\" id=\"humanscale-original\">{\"source\": \"Fikfak, Zbašnik Senegačnik & Drobne (2024) Urban Science 8: 257\", \"n\": 88, \"indicators\": [[\"I1\", \"Area connectivity\"], [\"I2\", \"Readability and completeness of the ambience\"], [\"I3\", \"Clarity and expressiveness of building design\"], [\"I4\", \"Complementarity of buildings, urban furniture, and other areas\"], [\"I5\", \"Presence of greenery\"], [\"I6\", \"Transparency of tree canopies\"], [\"I7\", \"Perception of artistic composition principles\"]], \"views\": [[\"N1\", \"Litostrojski bloki\"], [\"N2\", \"Štepanjsko naselje\"]]}</script>\n<style>\n:root{--bg:#eef1f3;--card:#fff;--ink:#1b2126;--muted:#5a636b;--accent:#2f5d7c;--line:#d6dde2;--warn:#b3261e;--sel:#dde9f2}\n*{box-sizing:border-box}html,body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);font:17px/1.5 system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,sans-serif}\nmain{max-width:820px;margin:0 auto;padding:22px 16px 40px}\nh1{font-size:1.5rem;margin:0 0 8px}h2{font-size:1.15rem;margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 12px;color:var(--muted)}\n.card{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;padding:18px;margin-top:14px}\n.btn{appearance:none;border:0;border-radius:10px;padding:13px 20px;font:inherit;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;background:var(--accent);color:#fff}\n.btn:disabled{opacity:.35;cursor:not-allowed}\n.prog{font-size:.88rem;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:8px}\n.win{border:10px solid #e9e4da;border-radius:6px;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 2px #cfc8bb;background:#e9e4da}\n.win img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}\n.def{background:var(--sel);border-radius:10px;padding:10px 12px;color:var(--ink);font-size:.95rem}\nlabel.opt{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:center;padding:9px 12px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;margin-top:6px;cursor:pointer}\nlabel.opt:has(input:checked){background:var(--sel);border-color:var(--accent)}\n.blk.miss{outline:2px solid var(--warn);outline-offset:4px;border-radius:8px}\n.err{color:var(--warn);margin-top:8px;min-height:1.2em}\n.credit{max-width:820px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 16px 24px;font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted)}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<main id=\"app\" aria-live=\"polite\"><p>Loading…</p></main>\n<footer class=\"credit\">Photographs, definition and indicators: Fikfak, Zbašnik Senegačnik &amp; Drobne (2024), Urban Science 8(4): 257, Figure 3 and Section 2.3 (doi:10.3390/urbansci8040257, CC BY 4.0).</footer>\n<script>\n(function(){\n  var KEY='window-humanscale:state', VIEWS=['N1','N2'];\n  var DEF='\\u201cHuman scale refers to a size, texture, and articulation of physical elements that match the size and proportions of humans and, equally important, correspond to the speed at which humans walk. Building details, pavement texture, street trees, and street furniture are all physical elements contributing to human scale.\\u201d (Ewing and Clemente)';\n  var app=document.getElementById('app'), Q={}, files={}, st=null;\n  function esc(s){return String(s==null?'':s).replace(/[&<>\"]/g,function(c){return {'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','\"':'&quot;'}[c];});}\n  function err(m){var e=app.querySelector('.err');if(e)e.textContent=m||'';}\n  function ok(r){return !(r&&r.ok===false);}\n  function save(){try{localStorage.setItem(KEY,JSON.stringify(st));}catch(e){}}\n  function send(list,b,next){if(b)b.disabled=true;Promise.all(list).then(function(rs){var bad=rs.filter(function(r){return !ok(r);})[0];if(bad){if(b)b.disabled=false;return err(bad.error);}next();});}\n  function fresh(){return {step:'intro',group:Math.random()<0.5?'SA1':'SA2',k:0};}\n  function intro(){\n    var multi=st.group==='SA2';\n    app.innerHTML='<h1>Window views</h1><p>Imagine you are at home, looking out of your window at the building opposite. You will see two such window views from residential neighbourhoods. For each view, say which '+(multi?'elements give':'element gives')+' the view its human scale.</p><p class=\"def\">'+esc(DEF)+'</p><p>'+(multi?'You may choose as many elements as you like for each view.':'Choose one element for each view.')+' It takes about 2 minutes.</p>'+\n     '<div class=\"card\"><label class=\"opt\" style=\"margin-top:0\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"ok\"> '+esc(Q.consent.title)+'</label><div style=\"margin-top:16px\"><button class=\"btn\" id=\"go\">Start</button></div><div class=\"err\"></div></div>';\n    document.getElementById('go').onclick=function(){if(!document.getElementById('ok').checked)return err('Consent is needed to continue.');\n      send([SPSite.answer('consent',true),SPSite.answer('group',st.group)],this,function(){st.step='view';st.k=0;save();route();});};\n  }\n  function view(){\n    if(st.k>=VIEWS.length){st.step='about';save();return route();}\n    var id=VIEWS[st.k],f=files[id],multi=st.group==='SA2',q=multi?Q.humanscale_multi:Q.humanscale_single;\n    app.innerHTML='<div class=\"prog\">Window view '+(st.k+1)+' of '+VIEWS.length+'</div><div class=\"win\"><img alt=\"Window view\" src=\"'+esc(f.url)+'\"></div>'+\n     '<div class=\"card\"><h2>'+esc(q.title)+'</h2><p style=\"margin:0;font-size:.9rem\">'+esc(DEF)+'</p><div class=\"blk\" data-n=\"ind\">'+(q.choices||[]).map(function(c){return '<label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"'+(multi?'checkbox':'radio')+'\" name=\"ind\" value=\"'+esc(c.value)+'\"> '+esc(c.text)+'</label>';}).join('')+'</div>'+\n     '<div style=\"margin-top:16px\"><button class=\"btn\" id=\"go\">'+(st.k<VIEWS.length-1?'Next view':'Continue')+'</button></div><div class=\"err\"></div></div>';\n    document.getElementById('go').onclick=function(){\n      var xs=[].slice.call(app.querySelectorAll('input[name=ind]:checked')).map(function(x){return x.value;});\n      if(!xs.length){app.querySelector('.blk').classList.add('miss');return err(multi?'Please choose at least one element.':'Please choose one element.');}\n      var a=multi?SPSite.answer('humanscale_multi',xs,{key:id,shown:[f.name]}):SPSite.answer('humanscale_single',xs[0],{key:id,shown:[f.name]});\n      send([a],this,function(){st.k++;save();route();});};\n  }\n  function about(){\n    var q=Q.field;\n    app.innerHTML='<h2>About you</h2><div class=\"card\"><div class=\"blk\" data-n=\"field\"><b>'+esc(q.title)+'</b>'+(q.choices||[]).map(function(c){return '<label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"field\" value=\"'+esc(c.value)+'\"> '+esc(c.text)+'</label>';}).join('')+'</div><div style=\"margin-top:16px\"><button class=\"btn\" id=\"go\">Finish</button></div><div class=\"err\"></div></div>';\n    document.getElementById('go').onclick=function(){var x=app.querySelector('input[name=field]:checked');if(!x){app.querySelector('.blk').classList.add('miss');return err('Please choose one.');}\n      send([SPSite.answer('field',x.value)],this,function(){st.step='done';save();route();});};\n  }\n  function finish(){\n    app.innerHTML='<h1>Thank you!</h1><div class=\"card\"><p id=\"fin\">Submitting…</p><div class=\"err\"></div></div>';\n    SPSite.complete().then(function(r){if(!ok(r)){err(r.error||'Some answers are missing.');setTimeout(function(){st.step='intro';save();route();},1800);}\n      else{try{localStorage.removeItem(KEY);}catch(e){}var s=document.getElementById('fin');if(s)s.textContent='Your answers are saved.';}});\n  }\n  app.addEventListener('change',function(e){var r=e.target.closest&&e.target.closest('.blk');if(r){r.classList.remove('miss');err('');}});\n  function route(){var s=st.step;window.scrollTo(0,0);if(s==='view')return view();if(s==='about')return about();if(s==='done')return finish();intro();}\n  SPSite.onReady(function(ctx){\n    ['consent','group','humanscale_single','humanscale_multi','field'].forEach(function(n){Q[n]=SPSite.getQuestion(n)||{};});\n    (SPSite.getMedia('views')||[]).forEach(function(f){files[f.name.replace(/\\.[^.]+$/,'')]=f;});\n    var need=VIEWS.filter(function(k){return !files[k];});\n    if(need.length){app.innerHTML='<h1>Images missing</h1><p>Upload '+esc(need.join(', '))+' (.jpg) to the media folder \"views\".</p>';return;}\n    try{st=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(KEY));}catch(e){st=null;}\n    var a=(ctx&&ctx.answers)||{};\n    if(!(st&&st.group)||a.consent!==true)st=fresh();\n    save();route();\n  });\n})();\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
